# SECRETS — must never enter a layer. Docker COPY does not read .gitignore, so without
# this line `COPY . .` bakes the Anthropic key into the image, where it survives every
# later RUN that "deletes" it and travels with the image to any registry it is pushed to.
.env
*.pem
*.key

# Bulk / rebuilt by the image
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.pytest_cache/

# Runtime artifacts: regenerated by scripts/prepare_deploy.py at build time. Copying a
# local ledger or catalog in would ship dev noise as if it were the demo's audit trail.
cases/*/ledger.jsonl
cases/*/catalog.json
cases/*/search_index.jsonl
cases/*/snapshots/
cases/*/sources/*.pdf
cases/*/sources/*.clauses.json

# EXCEPT the real Santa Cruz corpus: these PDFs are downloaded-and-OCR'd originals (not
# regenerable by a script) and its catalog/index are expensive to rebuild (OCR ingest
# peaks ~4GB RSS — more than a cloud builder gets). They ship pre-baked.
!cases/santacruz/sources/*.pdf
!cases/santacruz/catalog.json
!cases/santacruz/search_index.jsonl

# Docs/output, not runtime
*.md
!README.md
